# ARCHITECTURE — {{PROJECT_NAME}} architecture baseline

> The constitution of the **code** this company writes and maintains — the CLI, the
> skills, the product itself. Where `CONSTITUTION.md` governs how we work and
> `WORKFLOW.md` governs what we produce, this doc governs **how the code is allowed
> to be shaped**, and it carries that ruling *across* tasks.
>
> **Read on demand, not in the boot set** — loaded by whoever designs or changes
> code (usually `dev-maintainer`), before the design, not after the bug.
>
> **The one doc that holds three tenses apart.** Everywhere else, living docs are
> current-state interfaces (upgrade by replacement, no sediment). Here that rule is
> suspended on purpose: **CURRENT** (what the code *is*, with evidence) and
> **TARGET** (what new code *must obey*) are recorded side by side, and the
> evidenced distance between them is the **GAP ledger**. Writing a wish into
> CURRENT is the failure this separation exists to prevent.
>
> **Size it to the codebase.** A 300-line CLI deserves one screen: invariants +
> who-owns-what. Grow a partition only when the code earns it — the full shape and
> the bootstrap procedure for an already-drifted codebase live in
> `documentation/playbooks/architecture_baseline.md`.

